Replaces mpd5 with an in-kernel PPPoE driver (if_pppoe(4)) for eligible
PPPoE WAN interfaces, on OPNsense 25.7.x / FreeBSD 14.3, amd64, standalone
boxes only (no CARP/HA).

This plugin only records whether kernel mode is desired; applying a change
requires a reboot. It never switches a live session. On boot, if enabled,
early startup verifies the installed if-pppoe-kmod package matches the
running kernel build and offers the kernel features this plugin requires,
then hands eligible PPPoE interfaces to the kernel driver in place of mpd5.
Any check that fails, or any interface this plugin does not support (yet),
falls back to stock mpd5 automatically — nothing about your PPPoE
configuration in Interfaces -> Point-to-Point changes.

See Services -> Kernel PPPoE for the enable/exclude toggle, current hook
and per-interface backend status, and the Reboot action.

WWW: https://github.com/nashant/if_pppoe
